<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Darin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1915">1915</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Darin Pact</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Darin was signed on 26 December 1915 on the island of Tarut between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, represented by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/percy-cox">Percy Cox</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud</a>. Britain recognised his rule over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Najd</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">al-Hasa</a> and placed his lands under its protection, in return for his promise not to deal with other powers; he also received a subsidy. It was superseded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jeddah-1927">Treaty of Jeddah</a> in 1927.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-darin.jpg" alt="Treaty of Darin" width="279" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author, photo taken in 1916 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Percy_Cox_1916.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
